asio::co_spawn boost

c++ std::promise

asio::thread_pool

Exception Chain: exception propagation inside them

Namespace: [*`boost::asio`]

[h1:asio-co_spawn [role cyan asio::co_spawn]]

asio::co_spawn spawns a coroutine-based execution thread.

```
deduced_type asio::co_spawn(
	executor_or_context,
	awaitable_or_lambda,
	completion_token,
	constraint_ = 0
);
```

[*executor_or_context] can be an executor or an object of asio::io_context.

[*awaitable_or_lambda] can be an awaitable coroutine or a lambda object.

A lambda is a c++ object.

[*completion_token] is a token, which will handle the notification when the execution has completed.

[*Handler Signature]:

```
void(std::exception_ptr, T);
```

[*Token Signature]:

```
void(std::exception_ptr, T);
```

[h1:std-promise [role cyan std::promise]]

std::promise for cross-threading exception handling.

[h1:exception-chain [role cyan Exception Chain]]

Exception Chain: Exception Propagation

In my practice, the exception thrown in [*[role ddblue awaitable_or_lambda]] is propagated to [*[role ddblue completion_token]], which is managed by [*[role dblue asio::co_spawn]] itself. If the execution spawned by [*[role blue asio::co_spawn]] is a sub-thread, how to retrieve the exception from it? The way is [*[role dblue std::promise]] .

[h1:cpp-example [role cyan c++ Example]]

[!c++]
```
#include <boost/asio.hpp>
#include <future>
#include <iostream>
#include <random>

namespace asio = boost::asio;

namespace ut
{
	inline std::mt19937 rnd{std::mt19937_64{std::random_device{}()}()};
}

int main()
{
	asio::thread_pool pool{32u};
	std::promise<void> promise;
	std::future<void> future = promise.get_future();

	asio::co_spawn(
		pool.get_executor(),
		[]
			->
				asio::awaitable<void>
		{
			if (ut::rnd() %2 == 0)
				throw std::runtime_error{
					"Not an error: just a test."
				};
			std::cout << "OK\n";
			co_return;
		},
		[promise = std::move(promise)]
		(std::exception_ptr eptr)	// The completion token
			mutable
		{
			if (eptr)
				promise.set_exception(eptr);
			else
				promise.set_value();
		}
	);

	try
	{
		future.get();
	}
	catch (const std::exception & e)
	{
		std::cerr << "ERROR: " << e.what() << std::endl;
	}

	pool.join();
}
```

